WEBVTT

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.870
You like them?

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.460
They're mass-produced Argevollens:

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.240
Perphevollens.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.990
I'm sure you're already familiar with the name.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.620
Even if you mass-produce them, it will take too long to train the pilots.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:26.550
Did you forget

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.130
the system we experimented with at Cape Sagara?

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.220
Remote control of unmanned machines by a commander unit.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.740
That's right.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.980
That's the true nature of the U-Link system.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.620
If you pilot the commander unit,

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.920
you can control them as an extension of your own limbs.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.180
I reported

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.150
that Ingelmia was using a machine of the same type as Argevollen, did I not?

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:58.300
We know about Sturm Alpha.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.800
However,

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.810
it's nowhere near what we have.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.750
It's a cheap imitation.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.280
But, well...

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.840
We completed the Perphevollens by feeding back the data

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.210
from Sturm Alpha and Argevollen's fight.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.720
That's why you made Sturm fight Argevollen?

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.350
That's right.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.180
Everything you did was for this.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:27.160
Of course, when I heard you were going to stop using Argevollen,

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.180
I was worried.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:37.740
But what would come of making peace with Ingelmia now?

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.440
We'd lose our territory,

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.490
and the citizens would lose the land they were born on.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.250
Can you let that happen?

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.000
I can't.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.550
What of all the blood our soldiers shed?

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.000
Why did I send them to their deaths?

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:56.850
They

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.470
died to protect this country.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.860
We can't pretend that never happened and make peace...

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.390
I won't allow it.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:09.400
But that doesn't make it right to shed any more blood.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.870
Right?

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.900
That's why we're using these.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.320
How would you like to start a new war yourself?

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.450
Resolve

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.470
Isn't this what you should do?
Resolve

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.010
Isn't this what you should do?

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.030
Brings back memories, right?

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:28.050
I made it all look just like it did back then.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.790
But you don't want to see that, huh?

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.340
They're too fast!

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.360
Damn it! Charlie's down, too!

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:52.850
They're too fast to aim at!

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:16.750
Hey. I'm going out for a bit.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.420
Get it done by the time I get back.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:20.040
Where are you going?

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.830
My second wife lives nearby.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.300
She wants to see me about our kid's issues at school.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.880
It's not even my problem anymore...

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.880
Does she think I can act like a father now?

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.260
It's a mystery to me that he was able to get married three times.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:37.030
As a woman, I can't understand it.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.840
Must be into older people.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.590
What? They'd have to be retirement age!

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.820
No, I mean his wives.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.070
Oh, I see.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.990
Maybe he's actually really devoted.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.690
I could see that.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.840
Even when we're working, he always says,

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.860
"You have to treat a mech like a woman: carefully!"

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:58.000
And we always say, "Chief, that's sexual harassment!"

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.860
He talks tough,

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.750
but he teaches us well.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.710
But the biggest mystery

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:06.720
is how <i>we</i> don't even have boyfriends.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:14.640
Okay, we're online!
Where's that #12 wrench?
Work. Time to work.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:23.930
Huh?

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:24.650
What?

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:27.650
I thought the captain just passed by.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:30.340
He's not there.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:31.660
I must've been mistaken.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.160
We are <i>so</i> pathetic!

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.310
Where'd that come from?

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:39.750
You're skipping a few too many steps.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.030
No events ever happen for us!

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:46.670
Now that you mention it, standing by in the rear is boring.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:48.880
Why don't we throw an event, then?

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:49.920
I'm in!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.720
Okay, then let's...

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:22.250
Lorenz-san, is the Seiran's maintenance done?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:23.080
Dunno.

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:27.410
Okui-san!

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.840
So busy. So busy.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:36.510
Jamie!

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:39.930
W-We're just leaving.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.760
Huh? Leaving?

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:48.510
Bye!

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.580
Come on, Kaoru.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:50.560
We're gonna leave you.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:51.650
Wait!

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.120
Aren't they being too obvious?

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:58.700
Hey, Namie!

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:00.500
Listen...

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:03.120
S-S-Senpai!

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.000
Um, right...

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.910
Reports. Reports.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.000
Namie!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.220
We can decorate with stuff like this.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:10.880
What do you think?

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.640
Isn't that too flashy?

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.010
It looks like a pain.

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:16.090
You'll be helping.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.180
Yamanami-san,

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.750
what are you doing here?

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.120
And all you guys...

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.940
Well, gotta get to work.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.510
We need to hurry or the chief will yell at us.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:32.700
Okay, Yamanami.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.840
Come running with me.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.240
Okay.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.040
What? Did I do something?

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.200
Everyone's acting weird.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:46.850
Captain!

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:51.400
Keep this a secret from Tokimune,

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.010
but we're having a party to celebrate his recovery.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.160
I think it's a good idea.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.640
He'll be happy.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:01.270
Would you come, too, sir?

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.270
Sure thing.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:25.880
Okay, what's going on?

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.800
What are you all doing behind my back?

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.600
Or did I do something?

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.210
Did I?

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.460
Wait, wait, wait.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.590
What is it? Out with it!

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.590
Just wait, I said!

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:40.260
Are they all ignoring you, too, Jamie?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:43.470
"Too"? Are they ignoring you, as well?

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.240
Just us two?

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:48.230
Why?

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:49.820
I don't know.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:51.230
That's why I asked you!

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:54.730
Doesn't it feel like they're plotting something without us?

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:56.860
It does! But what?

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.950
I don't know!

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.900
What? You don't even know?

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.410
Then do you know?

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.370
I don't!

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:15.760
Private Susumu.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:17.380
What is it?

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.390
Have you seen the captain?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:20.890
No.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:27.140
Don't you think he's been acting strange lately?

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:30.430
Since you collapsed...

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:34.560
No, more precisely, since you decided to pilot Argevollen again.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.080
When I decided...

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.030
Yes.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:40.780
Was he that upset that I disobeyed orders?

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.690
Of course not, huh?

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:48.460
Oh.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.290
I met him in front of my sister's grave.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.760
He asked me what I thought

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.030
about piloting the system that killed my sister.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:57.300
What did you say?

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.530
I didn't know how to answer him.

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:03.500
But I said when I'm piloting Argevollen,

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:06.560
it feels like my sister is with me.

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:08.770
Like Reika-san is...

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:13.810
Crap.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:18.820
I should've asked her why everyone's ignoring me.

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:27.540
As twilight falls, the land turns the color of blood.

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:31.540
The soldiers' shadows lengthen as they walk.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:35.670
I wish their lives would lengthen like the shadows.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.430
But their lives are short.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:41.200
All that await them is eternal night.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:52.640
Samonji.

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:26.970
What we drink pales in comparison to this.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.850
How's Argevollen?

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:33.350
What do you mean?

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:37.490
You put a freeze on it once, but now you're using it again.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:40.860
Things are tight for us.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:43.740
We put on a show of bravado by freezing it,

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.600
but it's obvious we don't have enough firepower in a pinch.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.370
I gave up and decided to use it.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.500
You haven't changed.

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:58.190
That cynicism is just like you.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.960
When I met you earlier, I was worried something was wrong.

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:08.720
I called you here for one reason.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:12.920
Listen to me, Samonji.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:15.230
We're going to abandon this war.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.610
The politicians are looking to negotiate peace.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:24.100
It's all the enemy can do to maintain their overstretched supply lines.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:27.560
It'll be difficult for them to push the front lines forward any further.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:32.120
I heard units are gathering behind the front lines.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.550
Yes.

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:36.620
But we've determined that it's unlikely they'll attack.

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:39.630
They're putting pressure on us for peace talks?

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:45.610
Ingelmia doesn't want a long stalemate.

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:47.380
Nor does Arandas.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:50.850
If the war drags on and peace is disrupted,

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:54.080
the people will turn and attack the military.

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:57.390
We want peace before that happens.

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:01.280
It's not the best choice, but it's not the worst.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.640
It's a political conclusion.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.560
What of the blood that's been shed?

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.150
Don't say that.

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:11.340
It's not that I don't care about the sacrifices that have been made.

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:14.140
But I don't want to make any more sacrifices.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.790
I want to avoid that, no matter what.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.540
An army where no one dies, huh?

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.040
No, it's nothing.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:28.080
But the militarists aren't going to take this lying down.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.300
Brigadier General Cayenne, in particular.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:32.880
You're right.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.530
They're already working behind the scenes.

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:38.120
They seem to have some kind of scheme.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:41.090
If we could push back the front lines a little,

00:14:41.090 --> 00:14:45.370
we could quiet the militarists like Cayenne.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.450
I hate the fact that I can't do anything.

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:52.980
You haven't changed, either.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:56.720
I need a favor.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:07.510
Why is everybody ignoring me?

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:14.010
Captain!

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:28.160
Suzushiro-san was looking for you.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:30.280
I see.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.790
Is there something wrong with Arge?

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.230
As her brother,

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:42.180
there's something I want you to know.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:51.070
What Reika hoped to achieve by participating in the U-Link system project.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:55.420
She wanted to make an army where no one dies.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:57.570
That's what she said.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:15:59.750
An army where no one dies?

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:09.890
"An army where no one dies?"

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:12.690
What did you mean, Sis?

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:16.930
Huh?

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.120
Say, Arge...

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:45.190
What do you think?

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:46.560
About everyone...

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.070
About the captain...

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:01.660
What was that?

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.640
What's going on?

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:07.550
What are you gonna do to me?

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:09.060
What are you doing?

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.140
Wh-What?

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.800
We're celebrating your recovery.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:22.370
You didn't have to involve me!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:27.070
But if we'd told you, Tokimune would have found out.

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:29.040
And you've had a rough time, too,

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:29.620
so we're throwing you in.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.400
"Throwing me in"?

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:32.750
Come on, come on!

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:34.840
It's a surprise!

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:38.340
Wait, so the reason you were avoiding me...

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:39.700
Sorry.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.220
We all hid it because we wanted it to be a surprise.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:45.070
Oh, I'm glad.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.400
Thank you!

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:54.730
Well, to be honest, it's just a chance to take a break.

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:56.860
Huh? Where's the captain?

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:59.400
I don't see Suzushiro-san, either.

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:01.910
I'm sure the two of them are—

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:04.530
Oh, well. Let's get started.

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:06.530
Senpai, blow out the candle!

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:07.740
Okay!

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:46.710
Can't sleep?

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:49.400
You can't, either?

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:50.840
Something like that.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:54.500
By the time I finished writing my reports to HQ, it was this late.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:09.570
They all really got us good, huh?

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:11.210
You said it.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:12.820
They even involved me...

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:15.640
Oh, they sent me a picture. Want to see?

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:20.270
They're totally making fun of me.

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:24.160
No, they're not. They all like you.

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:25.410
Do they?

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:26.280
Yup.

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:32.160
I'm glad I came to the 8th Unit.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:33.660
Me, too.

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:38.670
I was really happy they threw that party.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:39.920
Yeah.

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:42.460
A lot's happened.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:47.470
I mean, a lot's happened since we met.

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:50.100
Where is this coming from?

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:53.450
I'm just saying a lot's happened.

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:56.000
But why, all of a sudden?

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.420
Is it all of a sudden?

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:00.560
What now?

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:03.070
You haven't changed a bit.

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:04.940
What?

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:09.950
The way you always say the weirdest things with a straight face.

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:12.200
It hasn't changed since we met.

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:14.860
People don't change that easily.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.200
You haven't changed a bit, either, Jamie.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:18.750
Haven't I?

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:19.760
You haven't!

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:21.240
You're still a brat.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:22.960
And you still abuse people.

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:24.480
And you still...

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.470
Never mind.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:36.660
I've changed.

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:38.600
Since I met you.

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.240
Since I became Argevollen's chief engineer...

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:43.540
Since I joined this unit.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:45.110
Well, then...

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.860
I've changed, too.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.210
Have you?

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:56.750
You think we'll look back on this night and laugh someday?

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:58.580
We will.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.200
As long as we're alive.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:01.520
As long as we're alive...

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.630
Sorry, I didn't mean it that way.

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:05.700
It's okay.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.740
I understand the risk.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:10.010
But I'm still going to pilot Arge.

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:12.430
I won't stop you anymore.

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:15.010
I'll support you to the best of my ability.

00:21:15.970 --> 00:21:18.480
The captain will understand, right?

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:19.680
I'm sure he will.

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:43.170
That machine

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.670
smelled like blood.

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:14.360
We gaze into each other's eyes, open our hearts.

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:20.580
A cycle of strength and weakness.

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:27.210
Your eyes must have adjusted somewhat.

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:33.880
Verbalize though I may,

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:41.680
I remember that I can't

00:22:41.680 --> 00:22:48.310
rationalize everything

00:22:48.310 --> 00:22:55.490
The world will change, as long as I remain courageous.

00:22:56.740 --> 00:23:03.500
The telepathy I wouldn't have discovered alone,

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:09.630
leads me ahead, behind your dazzling silouette.

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:17.010
But even so, I'll keep my unwavering gaze on you;

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:23.600
It'll reach you someday.

00:23:37.530 --> 00:23:40.490
Another Mind
